  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 231 PM MST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nSunday will start off chilly as skies clear overnight behind \nSaturday's system. Despite more sunshine, we will still have a cold \nairmass in place, which should keep highs down in the upper 30s to \nlower 40s. The flow aloft will start to turn more zonal Sunday \nonwards, which will increase the potential for strong winds in the \nwind prone areas once again. 700-mb height gradients are marginally \nsupportive for high winds in the Arlington/Elk Mountain area during \nthe day on Sunday, spreading eastward to the Laramie range wind \nprone areas Sunday night into Monday as surface pressure falls east \nof the range. Current probabilities are around 60 to 70% for the \nArlington area, and 50% for the I-80 Summit and Bordeaux areas. \nElsewhere, westerly flow will resume warm air advection as 700-mb \ntemperatures climb back above 0C Monday and remain there through at \nleast Wednesday. This should push highs back to around 5-10F above \nseasonal averages. Conditions look largely dry, though there may be \nanother round of light mountain snow around Monday into Tuesday with \na weak shortwave passing through.",
